  "definition": "Leaving a lane to make a [play](/term/play). Roaming lets a laner affect other parts of the map beyond their lane. Because a [player](/term/player) is not present in lane during a roam to catch a [wave](/term/wave) or stop their opponent from hitting their tower, roams come with an opportunity cost. Setting up a roam requires the laner to account for this potential minion loss, such as [crashing](/term/crash) a [slow push](/term/slow-push) or (as a support) warding for an ally.",
